---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import ContextPreview from '../components/ContextPreview.astro';
import libraryImage from '../assets/context-library.webp';
import { appDownloadUrl } from '../data/app-release';

const tools = ['search', 'read_file', 'list_concepts', 'get_links', 'find_captures', 'whats_new'];
---
<Base
  title="ContextCake — Project knowledge for your coding agent"
  description="Connect your docs, team decisions, and personal notes to Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor. ContextCake combines matching sections, with sources and conflicts attached."
>
  <main id="main-content" class="home">
    <section class="hero page-width" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Local context for coding agents</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Project knowledge.<br /><span>For your coding agent.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">ContextCake is a local app that connects your docs, team decisions, and personal notes to the AI tools you code with.</p>
        <p class="hero-detail">Set which sources take priority. Your agent can retrieve the relevant sections, with their sources and any disagreements attached.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href={appDownloadUrl} download><Icon name="download" size={17} /> Download for Mac</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/demo/">Explore demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <p class="install-note">Apple silicon · Signed &amp; notarized<br /><a href="/install/">Intel Mac, Linux &amp; WSL: install from source <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
      </div>
      <ContextPreview />
    </section>

    <div class="compatibility page-width" aria-label="Compatible AI tools">
      <p>Connect through MCP</p>
      <ul><li>Claude Code</li><li>Codex</li><li>Cursor</li><li>Claude Desktop</li></ul>
      <a href="/docs/getting-started/connect-an-agent/">And other MCP clients <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>

    <section id="how-it-works" class="workflow page-width" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="workflow-title">The decisions behind your code<br />aren’t all in your repo.</h2>
        <p>An architecture doc explains the database choice. A team runbook adds an exception. Your notes cover local setup. Handing an agent one file misses the rest. Pasting everything in leaves it to sort out the contradictions.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <span class="step-number">01</span>
          <h3>Connect the sources you use.</h3>
          <p>Add Markdown folders or GitHub repositories. Your files stay where you keep them. Start with a single source and add more when you need them.</p>
          <div class="step-art source-files" aria-label="Example source types"><span><Icon name="folder" size={17} /> Markdown folders</span><span><Icon name="github" size={17} /> GitHub repositories</span></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="step-number">02</span>
          <h3>Decide which source takes priority.</h3>
          <p>Order your sources. For matching sections, the higher source takes precedence. Sections it doesn’t define are inherited from the sources below.</p>
          <div class="step-art source-order" aria-label="Example priority: Personal, then Team, then Company"><span><i></i>Personal</span><span><i></i>Team</span><span><i></i>Company</span></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="step-number">03</span>
          <h3>Let your agent search and read.</h3>
          <p>Connect your AI tool through MCP. It can find the relevant context and read the combined result, including where each section came from.</p>
          <div class="step-art tool-call"><code>search</code><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><code>read_file</code><span class="tool-note">Sources included</span></div>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mechanic-note">This is the <strong>cascade</strong>: combine matching sections across sources, while keeping the other versions visible. <a href="/docs/concepts/merge-semantics/">Read the merge rules <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="inspection" aria-labelledby="inspection-title">
      <div class="page-width">
        <div class="section-intro inspection-intro">
          <div><h2 id="inspection-title">See exactly what<br />your agent can read.</h2><p>Browse the combined context in the app. Follow a section back to its file. Compare a disagreement before deciding what to change.</p></div>
          <a class="text-link" href="/demo/">Try it in the browser <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <figure class="product-image">
          <a href="/demo/" aria-label="Explore the ContextCake Library in the Web Demo"><Image src={libraryImage} alt="ContextCake Library showing the Primary database decision, its personal source and date, and the company’s alternate value alongside it." widths={[720, 1080, 1440]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 1200px" loading="lazy" /></a>
          <figcaption><span>ContextCake Library · Web Demo</span><span>Sample data, open to explore. No account required.</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="inspection-details">
          <article><h3>Disagreements stay in the result.</h3><p>Each section carries its source and a date when available. Conflicting versions remain attached, so the agent can see what’s contested. Source priority is explicit; newer text doesn’t silently win.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Related knowledge stays connected.</h3><p>Follow links between decisions, runbooks, and notes. ContextCake exposes those connections as a knowledge graph that both you and your agent can explore.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="control page-width" aria-labelledby="control-title">
      <div class="control-heading"><h2 id="control-title">Your files.<br />Your rules.</h2><p>Run ContextCake locally. Keep using Git and the editors you already know.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ContextCake/context-cake">Read the source on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="control-features">
        <article><h3>Local retrieval, open-source engine</h3><p>The core runs on Node.js with no runtime dependencies. ContextCake reads and combines your sources locally; the AI tool you connect receives the context it requests.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Review before sharing</h3><p>With capture enabled, preview a session finding before sharing it with the team. Promote reviewed captures into durable team context.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Bring an existing knowledge graph</h3><p>Advanced setups can connect a trusted MCP source that implements the ContextCake graph contract. Its content joins the same cascade as your files.</p><a href="/docs/guides/foreign-mcp-sources/">MCP source guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="faq page-width" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <h2 id="faq-title">A few practical details.</h2>
      <div class="questions">
        <details><summary>How does this fit with AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>Keep those files for instructions your coding tool loads directly. ContextCake adds a way to search and read knowledge across sources through MCP, including shared decisions and your own notes. You can include existing instruction files in a source; your tool’s native instruction-loading behavior stays the same.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Do I need to reorganize my docs?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>You can start with a folder of Markdown files. To combine versions of a document across sources, they need the same relative path (the concept ID) and matching section keys. Explicit section anchors give you precise control. ContextCake doesn’t infer that two unrelated files describe the same thing.</p><a href="/docs/concepts/okf-bundles/">How documents and sections match <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></details>
        <details><summary>Does my context leave my machine?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>Local sources are read and combined on your machine. When a connected AI tool requests context, that content is passed to the tool and is subject to its data handling. GitHub sources use GitHub; team sync uses the repository you configure. Only run MCP source commands and manifests you trust.</p><a href="/docs/concepts/trust-boundary/">Read the trust model <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></details>
        <details><summary>What can my agent do through MCP?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>Six read-only tools let it search, read combined context, list concepts, follow links, find captures, and catch up on changes. Capture tools are opt-in.</p><div class="mcp-tools">{tools.map((tool) => <code>{tool}</code>)}</div><a href="/docs/reference/mcp-tools/">MCP tool reference <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></details>
        <details><summary>What are Packs?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>Packs are optional collections of rules, templates, examples, and reference material for a specific kind of work. Inspect their files and add them as a source alongside your own knowledge.</p><a href="/packs/">Browse Packs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing page-width" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
      <div><h2 id="closing-title">Start with the docs<br />you already have.</h2><p>Add a folder, connect your coding agent, and ask it about your project.</p></div>
      <div><div class="actions"><a class="button button-primary" href={appDownloadUrl} download><Icon name="download" size={17} /> Download for Mac</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/demo/">Explore the demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><a class="closing-install" href="/install/">All install options <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
	.home {
		position: relative;
		color: var(--cc-text-body);
	}
	.home :is(h1,h2,h3,p,figure) {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.home :is(h1,h2,h3) {
		text-wrap: balance;
	}
	.home p {
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}
	.page-width {
		max-width: 1200px;
		margin-inline: auto;
		padding-inline: 40px;
	}
	.hero {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 80px);
		align-items: center;
		padding-block: 76px 64px;
	}
	.eyebrow {
		display: flex;
		gap: 10px;
		align-items: center;
		color: var(--cc-text-body);
		font-size: 14px;
		font-weight: 500;
		margin-bottom: 24px;
	}
	.eyebrow::before {
		content: '';
		width: 7px;
		height: 7px;
		background: var(--cc-layer-personal);
		border-radius: 50%;
	}
	h1 {
		font-size: clamp(40px, 4.2vw, 60px);
		line-height: 1.06;
		letter-spacing: -.035em;
		font-weight: 600;
		margin-bottom: 24px;
	}
	h1 span {
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
	}
	.hero-lede {
		max-width: 36ch;
		font-size: 21px;
		line-height: 1.5;
		margin-bottom: 13px;
	}
	.hero-detail {
		max-width: 46ch;
		font-size: 16px;
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
		margin-bottom: 28px;
	}
	.actions {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 12px;
	}
	.button {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 9px;
		padding: 12px 19px;
		min-height: 48px;
		box-sizing: border-box;
		border-radius: 7px;
		border: 1px solid var(--cc-border-strong);
		font-size: 15px;
		font-weight: 600;
		text-decoration: none;
		transition: background var(--cc-transition), border-color var(--cc-transition);
	}
	.button-primary {
		color: var(--cc-on-cta);
		background: var(--cc-cta);
		border-color: var(--cc-cta);
	}
	:global(body.theme-paper) .button-primary {
		color: var(--cc-on-cta);
	}
	.button-primary:hover {
		background: var(--cc-cta-hover);
		border-color: var(--cc-cta-hover);
	}
	.button-secondary {
		background: transparent;
		color: var(--cc-text);
	}
	.button-secondary:hover {
		background: var(--cc-surface-soft);
		border-color: var(--cc-text-muted);
	}
	.home .install-note {
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
		font-size: 12px;
		line-height: 1.9;
		margin: 16px 0 0;
	}
	.install-note a {
		color: inherit;
		text-underline-offset: 4px;
	}
	.compatibility {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 18px 24px;
		padding-block: 25px;
		border-block: 1px solid var(--cc-border);
	}
	.compatibility p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 13px;
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
	}
	.compatibility ul {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 16px 30px;
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		color: var(--cc-text);
		font-size: 17px;
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.compatibility a {
		font-size: 12px;
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.compatibility a:hover {
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
	.workflow {
		padding-block: 104px 84px;
		scroll-margin-top: 30px;
	}
	.section-intro {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr;
		gap: 70px;
		align-items: start;
		margin-bottom: 48px;
	}
	h2 {
		font-size: clamp(30px, 3vw, 42px);
		font-weight: 500;
		line-height: 1.15;
		letter-spacing: -.025em;
		margin-bottom: 20px;
	}
	.section-intro > p {
		max-width: 48ch;
		font-size: 17px;
		line-height: 1.7;
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}
	.steps {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		gap: 36px;
	}
	.steps li {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--cc-border-strong);
		padding-top: 21px;
		min-width: 0;
	}
	.step-number {
		font: 12px/1.5 var(--cc-font-mono);
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
		margin-bottom: 18px;
	}
	h3 {
		font-size: 20px;
		font-weight: 500;
		line-height: 1.3;
		letter-spacing: -.01em;
		margin-bottom: 12px;
	}
	.steps p {
		font-size: 15px;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
		margin-bottom: 25px;
	}
	.step-art {
		min-height: 84px;
		display: flex;
		gap: 8px;
		align-items: center;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-content: center;
		margin-top: auto;
	}
	.source-files > span {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 8px;
		font-size: 13px;
		padding: 8px 10px;
		border: 1px solid var(--cc-border-strong);
		border-radius: 5px;
	}
	.source-order {
		display: grid;
		gap: 5px;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr;
	}
	.source-order span {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 10px;
		font-size: 12px;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}
	.source-order i {
		width: 55px;
		height: 6px;
		border-radius: 2px;
		background: var(--cc-layer-personal);
	}
	.source-order span:nth-child(2) i {
		width: 75px;
		background: var(--cc-layer-team);
	}
	.source-order span:nth-child(3) i {
		width: 95px;
		background: var(--cc-layer-company);
	}
	.tool-call code {
		font: 12px/1.6 var(--cc-font-mono);
		color: var(--cc-text);
		padding: 7px 9px;
		background: var(--cc-surface-solid);
		border: 1px solid var(--cc-border-strong);
		border-radius: 5px;
	}
	.tool-note {
		width: 100%;
		font-size: 12px;
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
	}
	.mechanic-note {
		margin: 30px 0 0;
		padding-top: 23px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--cc-border);
		font-size: 13px;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
	}
	.mechanic-note strong {
		color: var(--cc-text-body);
		font-weight: 500;
	}
	.mechanic-note a {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-left: 10px;
		text-underline-offset: 4px;
	}
	.inspection {
		padding-block: 80px 70px;
		background: var(--cc-surface-soft);
		border-block: 1px solid var(--cc-border);
	}
	.inspection-intro {
		display: flex;
		align-items: end;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 30px;
		margin-bottom: 36px;
	}
	.inspection-intro h2 {
		margin-bottom: 16px;
	}
	.inspection-intro p {
		max-width: 53ch;
		font-size: 17px;
		line-height: 1.65;
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}
	.text-link {
		font-weight: 500;
		font-size: 15px;
		text-underline-offset: 5px;
	}
	.inspection-intro > a {
		flex: none;
		margin-bottom: 4px;
	}
	.product-image {
		margin: 0;
	}
	.product-image > a {
		display: block;
		border: 1px solid var(--cc-border-strong);
		border-radius: 9px;
		overflow: clip;
	}
	.product-image img {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
	}
	.product-image figcaption {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 5px 15px;
		padding-top: 12px;
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
		font-size: 12px;
	}
	.inspection-details {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 70px;
		margin-top: 42px;
	}
	.inspection-details p {
		max-width: 52ch;
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
		font-size: 15px;
		line-height: 1.7;
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}
	.control {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 100px;
		padding-block: 104px;
	}
	.control-heading h2 {
		font-size: clamp(40px, 4.3vw, 60px);
	}
	.control-heading p {
		max-width: 31ch;
		font-size: 18px;
		line-height: 1.65;
		margin-bottom: 24px;
	}
	.control-features article + article {
		margin-top: 28px;
		padding-top: 26px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--cc-border);
	}
	.control-features p {
		font-size: 15px;
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
		line-height: 1.7;
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}
	.control-features a {
		display: inline-block;
		font-size: 13px;
		margin-top: 10px;
		text-underline-offset: 4px;
	}
	.faq {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.6fr;
		gap: 70px;
		padding-block: 10px 96px;
	}
	.faq h2 {
		font-size: 30px;
	}
	details {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--cc-border-strong);
	}
	details:last-child {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--cc-border-strong);
	}
	summary {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 20px;
		list-style: none;
		padding-block: 20px;
		min-height: 24px;
		font-size: 16px;
		color: var(--cc-text);
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	summary::-webkit-details-marker {
		display: none;
	}
	summary > span {
		font-size: 22px;
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
		transition: transform var(--cc-transition);
	}
	details[open] summary > span {
		transform: rotate(45deg);
	}
	summary:hover {
		color: var(--cc-text-body);
	}
	details > div {
		padding: 0 30px 24px 0;
	}
	details p {
		font-size: 15px;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
		margin-bottom: 12px;
	}
	details a {
		font-size: 14px;
		text-underline-offset: 4px;
	}
	.mcp-tools {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 8px;
		margin: 16px 0;
	}
	.mcp-tools code {
		font: 12px/1.6 var(--cc-font-mono);
		padding: 4px 8px;
		border: 1px solid var(--cc-border-strong);
		border-radius: 4px;
	}
	.closing {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 40px;
		padding-block: 64px 72px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--cc-border-strong);
	}
	.closing p {
		max-width: 38ch;
		font-size: 17px;
		margin: 0;
	}
	.closing-install {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-top: 16px;
		font-size: 13px;
		text-underline-offset: 4px;
		color: var(--cc-text-muted);
	}
	@media (max-width: 1050px) {
		.hero {
			gap: 28px;
			padding-top: 50px;
		}
		h1 {
			font-size: 44px;
		}
		.hero-lede {
			font-size: 19px;
		}
		.section-intro {
			gap: 40px;
		}
		.steps {
			gap: 24px;
		}
		.control {
			gap: 60px;
		}
		.faq {
			gap: 40px;
		}
		.compatibility {
			justify-content: flex-start;
		}
	}
	@media (max-width: 760px) {
		.page-width {
			padding-inline: 24px;
		}
		.hero {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			padding-block: 45px 35px;
			gap: 32px;
		}
		.hero-copy {
			max-width: 540px;
		}
		h1 {
			font-size: clamp(38px, 7vw, 52px);
		}
		.eyebrow {
			margin-bottom: 18px;
		}
		.hero-detail {
			max-width: 50ch;
		}
		.compatibility {
			gap: 12px;
			padding-block: 24px;
		}
		.compatibility p {
			width: 100%;
		}
		.compatibility ul {
			gap: 10px 24px;
			font-size: 16px;
		}
		.compatibility > a {
			margin-top: 3px;
			width: 100%;
		}
		.workflow {
			padding-block: 64px 48px;
		}
		.section-intro {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 8px;
			margin-bottom: 30px;
		}
		.steps {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 26px;
		}
		.steps li {
			display: grid;
